  "system": {
    "description": "<p><em>Unless you decide it was taken elsewhere, a magical trinket lies buried amid the ashes and timbers of the Lykona cottage at Witch’s End, undamaged by fire and the passage of time. Made of copper, the item is a hollow cylinder with dancing fauns cut out of it.</em></p><p>When you place a candle in this zoetrope’s cylinder and turn the metal key attached to the base counterclockwise, the cylinder rotates, casting a luminous parade of dancing fauns on nearby surfaces. While the lit zoetrope turns, it clears all magical curses on creatures within Close range.</p><p>Key to Victory 1 of the Astromancer’s reading (roll 6): when Forlorne appears, a PC holding it gains 1d4 Hope.</p>",
